    "description": "Single bus fares on participating services in England outside London are capped at \u00a32 instead of \u00a33 from 1 January to 31 December 2027. The saving is the Treasury's costing (Table 6.1) shared out across households by their bus fare spending in England outside London: 10.0% of what that spending would be at \u00a33 fares (\u00a3230m, divided by 0.9 for operator participation, over \u00a32,557m of spending), for the days the cap runs: 1 January to 5 April 2027 in 2026-27 and 6 April to 31 December 2027 in 2027-28. London residents get \u00a30. The saving is counted as household income, a methodological choice: the official cost is a grant to bus operators. Spending is held fixed, with no extra travel.",
